{"id":"4a54594b19acae3d","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-df-zfc-descriptive3-borel-code.md","title":"ZFC Descriptive3 Borel Code","display":"df-zfc-descriptive3-borel-code — ZFC Descriptive3 Borel Code","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-descriptive3-borel-code","aliases":["58-df-zfc-descriptive3-borel-code"],"display":"df-zfc-descriptive3-borel-code — ZFC Descriptive3 Borel Code","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md]]","[[../batch08/58-df-zfc-order11-well-founded-relation.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-descriptive3-borel-code"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-descriptive3-borel-code</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-descriptive3-borel-code — ZFC Descriptive3 Borel Code"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"815e63e5071e7b58\" href=\"?note=815e63e5071e7b58\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"1038f84878b895b1\" href=\"?note=1038f84878b895b1\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-zfc-order11-well-founded-relation.md\">../batch08/58-df-zfc-order11-well-founded-relation.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,\\tau,c,T,\\ell,R_T\\in V\">\\(X,\\tau,c,T,\\ell,R_T\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S\\)</span> (topological-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"815e63e5071e7b58\" href=\"?note=815e63e5071e7b58\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcOrder11WellFoundedRelation}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcOrder11WellFoundedRelation}_S\\)</span> (well-founded-relation predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"1038f84878b895b1\" href=\"?note=1038f84878b895b1\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-zfc-order11-well-founded-relation.md\">../batch08/58-df-zfc-order11-well-founded-relation.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive3BorelCode}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive3BorelCode}_S\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}descriptive3\\text{-}borel\\text{-}code} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive3BorelCode}_S(X,\\tau,c)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(X,\\tau)\\land\\exists T,\\ell,R_T\\;\\Bigl(c=\\langle T,\\ell\\rangle\\land T\\subseteq\\omega^{&lt;\\omega}\\land\\varnothing\\in T\\land\\forall s\\in T\\;\\forall m\\leq|s|\\;(s{\\upharpoonright}m\\in T)\\land R_T=\\{\\langle u,v\\rangle\\in T^2:\\exists m&lt;|u|\\;(v=u{\\upharpoonright}m)\\}\\land\\mathrm{ZfcOrder11WellFoundedRelation}_S(R_T,T)\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\ell)=T\\land\\forall s\\in T\\;\\bigl((\\neg\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;(s^\\frown\\langle n\\rangle\\in T))\\to\\ell(s)\\in\\tau\\bigr)\\land\\forall s\\in T\\;\\bigl((\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;(s^\\frown\\langle n\\rangle\\in T))\\to\\ell(s)\\in\\{0,1\\}\\bigr)\\land\\forall s\\in T\\;\\bigl(\\ell(s)=0\\to\\exists!n\\in\\omega\\;(s^\\frown\\langle n\\rangle\\in T)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}descriptive3\\text{-}borel\\text{-}code} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcDescriptive3BorelCode}_S(X,\\tau,c)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(X,\\tau)\\land\\exists T,\\ell,R_T\\;\\Bigl(c=\\langle T,\\ell\\rangle\\land T\\subseteq\\omega^{&lt;\\omega}\\land\\varnothing\\in T\\land\\forall s\\in T\\;\\forall m\\leq|s|\\;(s{\\upharpoonright}m\\in T)\\land R_T=\\{\\langle u,v\\rangle\\in T^2:\\exists m&lt;|u|\\;(v=u{\\upharpoonright}m)\\}\\land\\mathrm{ZfcOrder11WellFoundedRelation}_S(R_T,T)\\land\\operatorname{dom}(\\ell)=T\\land\\forall s\\in T\\;\\bigl((\\neg\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;(s^\\frown\\langle n\\rangle\\in T))\\to\\ell(s)\\in\\tau\\bigr)\\land\\forall s\\in T\\;\\bigl((\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;(s^\\frown\\langle n\\rangle\\in T))\\to\\ell(s)\\in\\{0,1\\}\\bigr)\\land\\forall s\\in T\\;\\bigl(\\ell(s)=0\\to\\exists!n\\in\\omega\\;(s^\\frown\\langle n\\rangle\\in T)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Well-foundedness and topology now use their actual predicates; successor sets are expanded so the assertion no longer relies on an undefined <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Succ}_T\">\\(\\operatorname{Succ}_T\\)</span> operator.</li>\n<li>The strict-extension relation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R_T\">\\(R_T\\)</span> is a bound set of ordered pairs on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>; the former bare symbol <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\supsetneq\">\\(\\supsetneq\\)</span> was neither a sequence-prefix relation nor declared data.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md","status":"resolved",